{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-25T10:01:17.171Z","author":"fleet-wave-script","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e0d15f3cda6eb998be619306","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.282","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/assignee"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-25T10:01:17.171Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-09-25T10:01:17.141Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-09-25T10:01:17.141Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"Pinned the toolchain to 2026.9.23 and adopted the guarded pm-ops launcher"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"release:check and the CI health gate pass on 2026.9.23 with the launcher byte-identical to the template"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"release:check exits 0; the launcher test and the CI health block pass"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Pins: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.17 -> 2026.9.23, pm-changelog ^2026.9.16 -> 2026.9.23, pm-ops ^2026.9.13 -> 2026.9.23 (package.json and package-lock.json). Launcher: pm-ops template copied unchanged; test/prepare-merge-driver.test.ts proves byte identity and exercises every launcher branch in isolated checkouts. Removes the unit tests of the vendored launcher internals from test/quality-scripts.test.ts (that behaviour is tested in pm-ops) and adds test/prepare-merge-driver.test.ts to the coverage gate explicit test list. Fixes a blind spot in the statement (V8 block) gate: it credited a block only when another process reported a covering range, but V8 emits a nested range only where a count differs from its parent, so code another process ran inside a larger covered range was counted as never entered. A zero block is now credited when another process with block-level coverage has a count-positive innermost range enclosing it; a process that reported the block at zero, or that lacks block coverage, never vouches for it. The new module-level test fails on the previous gate. The CI health block runs green with --require-merge-drivers; release:check exits 0."}],"before_hash":"3868765e33b63c8845eb738c6a0193dbf5b344c11fe169808657905beb9c11b8","after_hash":"2556bb70b483ca2493476a0caf9e9f60143336f0f1344a5f1c207ef7a409442c","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c17a4498ac62ca1311ff4b00736a163065b09e4beb2b37e4707874469322d2c5"}
